WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:02.160
Every week, someone asks me the same

00:02.320 --> 00:02.720
question.

00:03.200 --> 00:05.200
Bert, how does this actually work?

00:05.680 --> 00:06.640
Where do we even start?

00:07.160 --> 00:09.440
So let's answer it once, clearly, for

00:09.520 --> 00:10.000
everyone.

00:10.400 --> 00:12.560
Players, parents, and our scouts too.

00:13.120 --> 00:15.440
At MFH Global Football, everything runs

00:15.560 --> 00:16.560
through five steps.

00:17.000 --> 00:19.200
The same five steps, in the same order,

00:19.560 --> 00:20.320
for every player.

00:20.920 --> 00:23.200
I'm Bert Mahecha, founder of MFH Global

00:23.280 --> 00:25.200
Football and a FIFA licensed agent.

00:25.680 --> 00:26.880
Let me walk you through each one.

00:27.440 --> 00:29.360
Step one is the questionnaire.

00:29.410 --> 00:30.800
You'll find it on our website, and it

00:30.880 --> 00:32.880
asks the same questions I would ask you

00:32.960 --> 00:34.480
if we were sitting down face to face.

00:35.040 --> 00:36.800
Who the player is, where they play,

00:37.120 --> 00:39.040
their position, their history, their

00:39.120 --> 00:39.760
eligibility.

00:40.280 --> 00:42.080
And if the player is under eighteen, a

00:42.240 --> 00:43.760
parent or guardian is part of it from

00:43.840 --> 00:44.320
the start.

00:44.840 --> 00:46.480
This step lets me get to know the player

00:46.640 --> 00:47.680
before we ever talk.

00:48.240 --> 00:50.400
Step two is the player profile, which

00:50.480 --> 00:51.840
you build on our partner platform,

00:52.080 --> 00:52.880
Analytic Soccer.

00:53.440 --> 00:55.360
This is your game, documented.

00:55.840 --> 00:57.840
Match footage, your playing history, and

00:57.920 --> 00:59.920
your position data, organized into a

01:00.000 --> 01:02.000
profile a club can actually read.

01:02.560 --> 01:04.320
Coaches and sporting directors are busy

01:04.680 --> 01:05.040
people.

01:05.150 --> 01:07.120
A clear, professional profile is how a

01:07.200 --> 01:09.120
player gets taken seriously.

01:09.330 --> 01:11.680
Step three is the evaluation, also done

01:11.760 --> 01:13.040
through Analytic Soccer.

01:13.120 --> 01:14.720
It's an honest read of where the player

01:14.800 --> 01:16.720
stands today, measured against real

01:16.840 --> 01:19.120
benchmarks and the player's age, not one

01:19.240 --> 01:21.600
good day or one bad day at a tryout.

01:21.650 --> 01:23.200
It shows what's ready and what still

01:23.280 --> 01:24.240
needs work.

01:24.320 --> 01:26.560
That honesty is a gift, because it gives

01:26.640 --> 01:28.720
every player a clear plan.

01:28.930 --> 01:30.720
Step four is the agent call.

01:30.830 --> 01:32.560
This is where you sit down with me.

01:32.640 --> 01:33.920
Because you've already completed the

01:34.000 --> 01:35.680
first three steps, I come into that

01:36.040 --> 01:37.760
conversation already knowing the player,

01:37.870 --> 01:39.920
the footage, and the evaluation.

01:40.040 --> 01:41.120
So we don't spend our time on the

01:41.200 --> 01:41.920
basics.

01:42.000 --> 01:44.000
We spend it on your future.

01:44.110 --> 01:45.200
This is where FIFA licensed

01:45.280 --> 01:47.920
representation begins: contracts,

01:48.030 --> 01:50.160
compliance, and someone whose job is to

01:50.360 --> 01:51.600
protect the player.

01:51.810 --> 01:53.760
Step five is the opportunity.

01:53.870 --> 01:55.440
This is where doors open.

01:55.560 --> 01:57.680
A professional club, a trial, a

01:57.760 --> 01:59.920
transfer, or a college program.

02:00.000 --> 02:01.760
And every one of those opportunities is

02:01.840 --> 02:04.640
pursued the right way, within the rules.

02:04.800 --> 02:06.720
Why does the order matter so much?

02:06.930 --> 02:08.400
Because each step builds on the one

02:08.480 --> 02:09.360
before it.

02:09.410 --> 02:11.360
When a player skips ahead, everyone is

02:11.440 --> 02:12.160
guessing.

02:12.240 --> 02:14.240
When a player follows the steps, every

02:14.560 --> 02:15.920
conversation is built on real

02:16.440 --> 02:18.400
information, and every opportunity we go

02:18.480 --> 02:21.120
after fits who that player really is.

02:21.440 --> 02:23.120
Now, a word to our scouts.

02:23.230 --> 02:24.880
When you find a player you believe in,

02:24.990 --> 02:26.080
your job is simple.

02:26.130 --> 02:27.720
Start them at step one, the

02:27.730 --> 02:29.650
questionnaire, and let the steps do

02:29.730 --> 02:30.210
their work.

02:30.690 --> 02:33.090
Please don't promise a club, a trial, or

02:33.140 --> 02:35.250
a contract, and don't send anyone

02:35.330 --> 02:36.850
straight to a call with me before the

02:36.930 --> 02:38.130
first three steps are done.

02:38.690 --> 02:40.450
If the player is a minor, the parents

02:40.530 --> 02:42.290
are part of the process from day one.

02:42.850 --> 02:44.450
When you follow the five steps, you

02:44.530 --> 02:46.210
protect the player, you protect the

02:46.410 --> 02:48.370
family, and you protect the name every

02:48.450 --> 02:49.330
one of us works under.

02:49.930 --> 02:51.410
And to the players and parents watching:

02:51.970 --> 02:53.730
these five steps aren't hoops to jump

02:53.810 --> 02:53.970
through.

02:54.490 --> 02:55.730
They're how we make sure that when the

02:55.810 --> 02:57.810
right opportunity shows up, you're ready

02:57.890 --> 02:58.130
for it.

02:58.690 --> 02:59.650
So here's your next step.

03:00.170 --> 03:01.490
Go to our website and start the

03:01.570 --> 03:02.530
questionnaire.

03:02.580 --> 03:03.810
I look forward to getting to know you.
